# License of this repository

This repository is **dual-licensed by path**. The legal texts are in the two files
named below; this file only states the split, so that no reader has to guess whether
the evidence data is MIT.

| What | Where | License | Notice file |
|---|---|---|---|
| Text, tables, figures, transcripts quoted in the paper, and the evidence data | the whole repository except the two rows below | **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0** (CC-BY-4.0) | `LICENSE-content.md` |
| Executable tooling | `scripts/`, `tools/` | **MIT License** | `LICENSE-code.md` |
| Third-party material inside the evidence | IDE screenshot (`evidence/screenshots/`), provider error strings, model and product names | remains the rights holder's; cited for identification and commentary | see `LICENSE-content.md` |

**Attribution for reuse:** `2makeitwork, "AI Service QoS — Independent Measurement of
What Users Actually Receive", <release tag or commit>, 2026.` State the collection
round and the client version, not only the model name.

**A note on machine-readable license fields.** The dataset card front matter declares
`license: cc-by-4.0` because the dataset repository ships data and text only; the
tooling under `scripts/` and `tools/` keeps its MIT notice in the source repository.
`CITATION.cff` carries the same split, and `scripts/verify_dataset_card.py` fails if
the three documents disagree.
